["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>The rifle is zeroed from a bench. Deer are shot from dirt, snow and sticks. The gap between the two is the shot you miss.</p></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 440\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"440\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Four positions, steadiest first</text>\n\n  <!-- 1 Prone -->\n  <g transform=\"translate(10,40)\">\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"185\" height=\"172\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text>\n    <text x=\"38\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Prone</text>\n    <text x=\"38\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Steadiest</text>\n    <line x1=\"10\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"175\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n    <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\n      <path d=\"M60 122 L115 132 L165 126 M115 132 L168 144\"/>\n      <path d=\"M62 124 L78 140 L92 112 M62 124 L70 140 L74 118\"/>\n    </g>\n    <circle cx=\"50\" cy=\"118\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n    <line x1=\"66\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"152\" y2=\"98\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n    <text x=\"10\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#23261f\">Both elbows on the ground</text>\n  </g>\n\n  <!-- 2 Sitting -->\n  <g transform=\"translate(205,40)\">\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"185\" height=\"172\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text>\n    <text x=\"38\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Sitting</text>\n    <text x=\"38\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Steady</text>\n    <line x1=\"10\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"175\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n    <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\n      <path d=\"M85 132 L92 86 M85 132 L118 106 L138 140 M85 132 L112 112 L130 140\"/>\n      <path d=\"M92 90 L116 108 L124 88 M92 90 L104 112 L100 92\"/>\n    </g>\n    <circle cx=\"94\" cy=\"74\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n    <line x1=\"96\" y1=\"96\" x2=\"172\" y2=\"76\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n    <text x=\"10\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#23261f\">Elbows inside the knees</text>\n  </g>\n\n  <!-- 3 Kneeling -->\n  <g transform=\"translate(10,220)\">\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"185\" height=\"172\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text>\n    <text x=\"38\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Kneeling</text>\n    <text x=\"38\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Less steady</text>\n    <line x1=\"10\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"175\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n    <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\n      <path d=\"M85 118 L90 76 M85 118 L118 100 L122 140 M85 118 L70 138 L42 140\"/>\n      <path d=\"M90 80 L116 98 L124 78 M90 80 L104 100 L100 82\"/>\n    </g>\n    <circle cx=\"92\" cy=\"64\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n    <line x1=\"94\" y1=\"86\" x2=\"172\" y2=\"66\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n    <text x=\"10\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#23261f\">One elbow on the knee</text>\n  </g>\n\n  <!-- 4 Standing -->\n  <g transform=\"translate(205,220)\">\n    <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"185\" height=\"172\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"18\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"18\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text>\n    <text x=\"38\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Standing</text>\n    <text x=\"38\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Hardest</text>\n    <line x1=\"10\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"175\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n    <g fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\n      <path d=\"M98 140 L111 98 L124 140 M111 98 L114 56\"/>\n      <path d=\"M114 60 L128 84 L140 62 M114 60 L122 80 L120 64\"/>\n    </g>\n    <circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"44\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n    <line x1=\"110\" y1=\"66\" x2=\"176\" y2=\"49\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n    <!-- sticks -->\n    <path d=\"M160 140 L146 58 M160 140 L172 58 M160 140 L158 58\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n    <text x=\"10\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#23261f\">No support. Add sticks</text>\n  </g>\n\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"418\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sticks or a tripod make 3 and 4 much steadier.</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"434\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ranking: Hunter Ed, national course. Figures not to scale.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Steadiest first: prone, sitting, kneeling, standing <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>A rest beats a position. Sticks make standing work (Tip).</li><li>Your max range is a number you tested, not a feeling (opinion).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all key points</summary><ul><li>Four standard rifle positions: prone, sitting, kneeling, standing. Prone is the steadiest. Standing is the hardest <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Get closer if you can. Get steadier if you can. A rest beats a position (Tip).</li><li>Sticks or a tripod turn a standing shot into a real option in tall grass and brush <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Five fundamentals: aiming, breath control, movement control, trigger control, follow through <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Dry fire builds the trigger press for free. Tikka says use a snap cap <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Your max ethical range is a number you tested, not a feeling. The 20 cm test is on a later screen (Hunt Mentor method, opinion).</li><li>Four weeks and about 60 rounds gets a beginner there (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"4\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Four positions, step by step</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 4</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Prone position: lying flat behind the rifle, both elbows on the ground, body straight behind the rifle. The steadiest position.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">1  Prone: steadiest</text><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"232\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"232\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"268\" cy=\"196\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3.5\"/><path d=\"M256 206 L160 222 L70 230\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M160 222 L80 224\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M254 208 L282 230 L304 204\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M250 210 L232 230 L262 204\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"246\" y1=\"204\" x2=\"360\" y2=\"186\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"372\" cy=\"184\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"372\" cy=\"184\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"282\" cy=\"230\" r=\"7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"232\" cy=\"230\" r=\"7\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Both elbows on the ground</text><line x1=\"246\" y1=\"66\" x2=\"234.0\" y2=\"220.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M230.7 211.6 L234.0 220.0 L238.5 212.2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\">Body straight behind the rifle</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\">Needs flat, open ground</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Best for learning: easiest to hold still</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Prone: lie flat, both elbows down.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Sitting position: seated, knees up, both elbows resting inside the knees, rifle level at the target.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">2  Sitting: next steadiest</text><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"240\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"240\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"206\" cy=\"160\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3.5\"/><path d=\"M200 172 L170 236\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M170 236 L232 198 L262 238\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M172 234 L226 204 L250 238\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M200 176 L228 204 L252 176\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M198 178 L220 206 L230 182\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"202\" y1=\"172\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"158\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"356\" cy=\"156\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"356\" cy=\"156\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"226\" cy=\"204\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Elbows inside the knees</text><line x1=\"232\" y1=\"58\" x2=\"224.0\" y2=\"194.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M220.6 185.7 L224.0 194.0 L228.4 186.1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"86\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\">Flat of the arm on the soft knee,</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"106\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\">not elbow point on the kneecap</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Tip: face downhill on a slope, it feels like a bench</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Sitting: elbows inside the knees.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Kneeling position: sitting on the heel of the rear foot, support elbow resting on the raised front knee.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">3  Kneeling: fast, clears low brush</text><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"246\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"246\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"190\" cy=\"136\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3.5\"/><path d=\"M186 148 L166 214\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M166 214 L150 246 L122 246\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M166 214 L226 204 L230 246\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M186 152 L224 198 L248 160\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M184 154 L204 186 L214 158\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"188\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"138\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"346\" cy=\"136\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"346\" cy=\"136\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><circle cx=\"224\" cy=\"198\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"160\" cy=\"236\" r=\"9\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"244\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Support elbow</text><text x=\"244\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">on front knee</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Sit on the heel</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">of the rear foot</text><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"98\" x2=\"152.0\" y2=\"228.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M144.4 223.2 L152.0 228.0 L151.0 219.1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Only one arm braced: less steady than sitting</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Kneeling: sit on your heel, elbow on the knee.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Standing with three leg shooting sticks: stick top at armpit height or a little lower, two legs toward you and one toward the target, feet square to the rifle, back of the hand resting on the sticks.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">4  Sticks: makes standing work</text><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"264\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"264\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"176\" cy=\"92\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"3.5\"/><path d=\"M176 104 L172 184\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M172 184 L160 262\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M172 184 L186 262\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M178 110 L214 136 L246 118\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M176 112 L190 140 L196 116\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M246 120 L214 262\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M246 120 L236 264\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M246 120 L300 262\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"180\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"104\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"356\" cy=\"102\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"356\" cy=\"102\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"258\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Top at armpit</text><text x=\"258\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">height or lower</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Feet square</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">to the rifle</text><text x=\"206\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Two legs toward you, one toward the deer</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Sticks: two legs to you, one to the deer.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>Prone is steadiest, standing is hardest <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Offhand only when the deer is close and there is no time to sit (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: details for each position</summary><ul><li><strong>Prone.</strong> Flat on the ground, both elbows down. The steadiest of the four. Best for learning the fundamentals because it is easiest to hold <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.<ul><li>Needs flat, open ground. Grass and sage block the view at deer height (Tip).</li></ul></li><li><strong>Sitting.</strong> Both arms supported by your legs. Next to prone, the steadiest <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.<ul><li>Elbows go inside the knees, bone against the soft inside of the knee, not elbow point on kneecap (Tip).</li><li>Face downhill on a slope and sitting becomes almost a bench (Tip).</li></ul></li><li><strong>Kneeling.</strong> Only one arm braced. Less steady than prone and sitting <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.<ul><li>Fast to get into. Gets your scope above low brush (Tip).</li><li>Sit on the heel of your rear foot. Rest the support elbow on the raised knee (Tip).</li></ul></li><li><strong>Standing (offhand).</strong> Neither arm supported. The most difficult position for an accurate shot <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.<ul><li>Do not try to stop the wobble. Keep it small and smooth <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Beginner rule: offhand only when the animal is close and there is no time to sit (Tip).</li></ul></li></ul></details><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=l-lzvjGPgKE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>Shooting Positions in the Field | Long-Range Rifle Shooting with Ryan Cleckner</b><small>Get as low and steady as the terrain allows.<br>NSSF—The Firearm Industry Trade Association, YouTube, 7 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Av7dexTSZt4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>Prone Position: Getting Set on the Rifle | Long-Range Rifle Shooting with Ryan Cleckner</b><small>Prone is the steadiest field position. Learn it first.<br>NSSF—The Firearm Industry Trade Association, YouTube, 3 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view of three leg shooting sticks: one leg points toward the target, two legs spread toward the shooter. The shooter stands with feet nearly square to the rifle.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Three leg sticks, seen from above</text><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"200.0\" y2=\"46.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M203.9 54.1 L200.0 46.0 L196.1 54.1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"212\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Target</text><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"96\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"196\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"196\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"96\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"196\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"196\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"150\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><ellipse cx=\"178\" cy=\"248\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"20\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"222\" cy=\"248\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"20\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Two legs</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"223\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\">toward you</text><text x=\"270\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">One leg toward</text><text x=\"270\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\">the target</text><text x=\"270\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Your feet: nearly</text><text x=\"270\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\">square, not bladed</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Your legs are the rear bipod</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Sticks make standing stable and stretch your range <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Top at armpit height or a bit lower. Feet square <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Carry the rest you practised with (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: sticks, bipods and natural rests</summary><ul><li>Standing is the least stable position. Sticks improve stability and increase your effective range while standing <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Three leg sticks: two legs toward you, spread, third leg toward the target. Height about your armpit or a little lower <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Set your feet nearly square to the rifle, not bladed like a pistol stance. Your legs are the rear bipod <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Hold the forend as normal and rest the back of your hand on the sticks. Most control, fastest second shot <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>A rifle mounted bipod works prone and sitting, or braced against a tree <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Natural rests: a tree, a pack, a rock. Hard rests can shift the shot high, soft rests low. Learn yours on paper <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Carry the rest you practised with. A tripod you have never dry fired from is a surprise at the worst time (Tip).</li></ul><aside class=\"callout lean\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>Buy a 3 leg trigger style shooting stick for the first season. It works standing and sitting, and doubles as a walking stick on the hill. Price checked 2026-10-01: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> in the gear session.</p></aside></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: the breath meter fills as you breathe in, then drops to half as you let half out. You hold. The crosshair wobble shrinks and settles on the lungs. The finger pad squeezes the trigger slowly, the shot breaks, and you hold still to call the shot.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Breathe, hold, squeeze, follow through</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"50\" width=\"40\" height=\"160\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"32\" y=\"208\" width=\"36\" height=\"0\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"><animate attributeName=\"y\" values=\"208;52;130;130\" keyTimes=\"0;.22;.38;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animate attributeName=\"height\" values=\"0;156;78;78\" keyTimes=\"0;.22;.38;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></rect><line x1=\"26\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"74\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"50\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Breath</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\">half</text><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"130\" r=\"70\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><g transform=\"translate(150 130)\"><ellipse cx=\"10\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"54\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><ellipse cx=\"-12\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" fill-opacity=\".35\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"62\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"198\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"82\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"218\" y2=\"130\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"-28 6;-2 -10;-24 12;0 2;-26 -8;-10 4;-16 -2;-12 2;-14 0;-12 1;-12 1\" keyTimes=\"0;.1;.2;.3;.38;.48;.56;.62;.68;.75;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><path d=\"M330 230 q 0 26 18 30\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><g><ellipse cx=\"318\" cy=\"240\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#e8c4a0\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;0 0;10 0;10 0\" keyTimes=\"0;.6;.78;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><text x=\"260\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#23261f\">Finger</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"260\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#23261f\">pad</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Wobble shrinks</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">when you hold</text><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1;0\" begin=\"7s\" dur=\".6s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"180\" font-size=\"24\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#e8590c\">BANG</text></g><text x=\"236\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\">1 Breathe in<set attributeName=\"fill\" to=\"#e8590c\" begin=\"0s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text><text x=\"236\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\">2 Let half out<set attributeName=\"fill\" to=\"#e8590c\" begin=\"2s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text><text x=\"236\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\">3 Hold<set attributeName=\"fill\" to=\"#e8590c\" begin=\"3.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text><text x=\"236\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\">4 Squeeze slowly<set attributeName=\"fill\" to=\"#e8590c\" begin=\"5.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text><text x=\"236\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\">5 Hold still,<set attributeName=\"fill\" to=\"#e8590c\" begin=\"7.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text><text x=\"236\" y=\"204\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\">call the shot<set attributeName=\"fill\" to=\"#e8590c\" begin=\"7.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Breathe in, half out, hold, squeeze, follow through. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Let about half the breath out, hold, squeeze <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Trigger on the pad of the finger. Slow, steady pressure <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Call your shot: where was the crosshair when it broke? (Tip)</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the full trigger and breath rules</summary><ul><li>Draw a deep breath. Let about half out. Hold it while you squeeze <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Held too long? Your pulse rises and the rifle moves. Take another breath and start over <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Trigger finger: the trigger rests on the pad, between the first joint and the fingertip <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Slow, steady pressure until the rifle fires. Jerking the trigger or clenching the hand moves the gun enough to miss <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Follow through: keep the squeeze and the sight picture until the bullet has left the barrel <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Hold your aim: put any movement on the target and keep the area of movement small <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>B.R.A.S.S.: Breathe, Relax, Aim, Squeeze, Squeeze more. A common memory aid <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Call your shot. Say where the crosshair was when the shot broke. If you cannot, you blinked (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Safe dry fire setup: rifle with an orange snap cap in the chamber aimed at a small dot on a basement wall 5 metres away. All ammunition is out of the room.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Safe dry fire setup</text><rect x=\"20\" y=\"50\" width=\"250\" height=\"200\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"250\" y=\"50\" width=\"20\" height=\"200\" fill=\"#c9b79c\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"260\" cy=\"130\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Basement wall</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">2 cm dot at 5 m</text><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"140\" y2=\"140\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><rect x=\"132\" y=\"134\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\">Snap cap in the chamber</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">(orange)</text><line x1=\"140\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"248.0\" y2=\"131.0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><path d=\"M242.3 135.1 L248.0 131.0 L241.3 129.1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"300\" y=\"110\" width=\"70\" height=\"44\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"335\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">AMMO</text><path d=\"M305 102 L365 162 M365 102 L305 162\" stroke=\"#b3261e\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"335\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Out of</text><text x=\"335\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">the room</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Never a window or a door as the backstop</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Dry fire is only safe with zero ammunition in the room. Every session. No exceptions.</p></aside><ul><li>Snap cap in, real backstop, 10 slow presses per position (Tip).</li><li>10 minutes, 3 evenings a week (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the 6 dry fire steps</summary><ol><li>Take every round out of the room. Magazine empty. Pockets empty (Tip).</li><li><button class=\"term\" data-term=\"PROVE\">PROVE</button> the rifle safe: Point, Remove, Observe, Verify, Examine <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Put a snap cap in the chamber. Tikka's manual says long term dry firing may damage the bolt and tells you to use a snap cap. Spring loaded \"primers\" are ideal <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Pick an aim point with a real <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Backstop\">Backstop</button>: a basement wall, never a window or a door (Tip).</li><li>Ten slow presses per position: prone, sitting, kneeling, sticks. Watch the crosshair at the click. It must not jump (Tip).</li><li>Say \"finished\" out loud. Snap cap out. Rifle locked away before ammunition comes back in (Tip).</li></ol><ul><li>Ten minutes, three evenings a week, is plenty (Tip).</li><li>Target: a 2 cm dot at 5 m. From sitting it should sit still through the click within two weeks (Tip).</li><li>Dry fire from the sticks too. One writer's wife dry fired from sticks for a week of evenings, then made a clean 200 yd shot from them on her hunt <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Week</th><th>Range (live)</th><th>Home (dry)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Zero at 100 m, then prone</td><td>Learn positions</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Prone, sitting, sticks at 100 m</td><td>Sticks nightly</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>150 m, one group at 200 m</td><td>3 nights</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Max range test</td><td>Rest</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>About 60 rounds in 4 weeks (Tip).</li><li>First 3 shots each session are cold and count (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the full week by week plan</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Week</th><th>At the range (live)</th><th>At home (dry)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Zero at 100 m (109 yd) from the bench, 10 rounds. Then 5 rounds prone</td><td>Learn each position. 10 min, 3 nights</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>15 rounds at 100 m: 5 prone, 5 sitting, 5 from sticks. Aim at a 20 cm circle</td><td>Sticks every night. Mount from carry</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>15 rounds: sitting and sticks at 150 m (164 yd), kneeling at 100 m. One 3 shot group at 200 m (219 yd) if the range allows</td><td>10 min, 3 nights</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Max range test, next screen. 9 to 12 rounds cold. Finish with 3 rounds to confirm zero</td><td>2 nights only. Rest before the hunt</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Total: about 60 rounds, 3 boxes of your hunting load (Tip). Prices are in the ammo session.</li><li>Every live session: the first 3 shots are cold and count. Write the result in the journal (Tip).</li><li>Shoot with the clothes you will hunt in. A thick jacket changes the stock fit (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: three cold shots land inside the 20 centimetre plate at 100 metres, tick. Three more inside at 150 metres, tick. At 200 metres one shot misses the plate, cross. The 250 metre plate is not shot. Result: your max ethical range is 150 metres.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">Max range test: 3 cold shots per plate</text><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"130\" r=\"34\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">100 m</text><circle cx=\"155\" cy=\"130\" r=\"34\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"155\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">150 m</text><circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"130\" r=\"34\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"250\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">200 m</text><circle cx=\"345\" cy=\"130\" r=\"34\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"345\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#23261f\">250 m</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">20 cm paper plate</text><circle cx=\"52\" cy=\"124\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#23261f\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"0.6s\" dur=\"0.2s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></circle><circle cx=\"66\" cy=\"134\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#23261f\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"1.15s\" dur=\"0.2s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></circle><circle cx=\"58\" cy=\"140\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#23261f\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"1.7s\" dur=\"0.2s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></circle><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2.25s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><path d=\"M46 228 L55.3 237.8 L74 216.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2e7d32\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></g><circle cx=\"165\" cy=\"120\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#23261f\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2.75s\" dur=\"0.2s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></circle><circle cx=\"143\" cy=\"136\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#23261f\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"3.3s\" dur=\"0.2s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></circle><circle cx=\"159\" cy=\"144\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#23261f\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"3.8499999999999996s\" dur=\"0.2s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></circle><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"4.3999999999999995s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><path d=\"M141 228 L150.3 237.8 L169 216.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2e7d32\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/></g><circle cx=\"240\" cy=\"122\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#23261f\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"4.8999999999999995s\" dur=\"0.2s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></circle><circle cx=\"262\" cy=\"140\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#23261f\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"5.449999999999999s\" dur=\"0.2s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></circle><circle cx=\"280\" cy=\"96\" r=\"4.5\" fill=\"#23261f\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"5.999999999999999s\" dur=\"0.2s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></circle><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6.549999999999999s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><path d=\"M238 216 L262 240 M262 216 L238 240\" stroke=\"#b3261e\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6.549999999999999s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"284\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#b3261e\">miss</text></g><g opacity=\"1\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;.3\" begin=\"7.049999999999999s\" dur=\".5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><circle cx=\"345\" cy=\"130\" r=\"34\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"7.049999999999999s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><text x=\"345\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">stop</text></g><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"7.649999999999999s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"70\" y=\"250\" width=\"260\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\">Your max: 150 m</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Last distance with all 3 hits is your max. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>20 cm plate, cold, from sitting or sticks, 90 seconds (opinion).</li></ul><ul><li>One miss: your max is the previous distance (Tip).</li></ul><ul><li>Cap it at 250 m (273 yd) your first season (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how to run the test</summary><aside class=\"callout lean\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>This is Hunt Mentor's method, an opinion, not a law. It is stricter than most hunters' habits on purpose.</p></aside><ul><li>Target: a <strong>20 cm circle</strong>. A paper plate. Deer vitals are about 20 to 25 cm (8 to 10 in) across, so the plate gives margin <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><strong>Cold.</strong> First shots of the day. No warm up, no sighters. A deer gives you none (Tip).</li><li><strong>Field position.</strong> Sitting or sticks, whichever you will really use. Not the bench (Tip).</li><li><strong>Timed.</strong> From standing with the rifle slung: get down, 3 shots, 90 seconds (Tip).</li><li>Start at 100 m. All 3 inside the circle? Move to 150 m. Repeat. Then 200 m, then 250 m.</li><li>The last distance where all 3 hit is your max ethical range. One miss and your max is the previous distance (Tip).</li><li>Cap it at 250 m (273 yd) for your first season, even if you pass (Tip).</li><li>Wind day? Take 50 m off. At 250 m a 20 km/h crosswind moves a 150 gr .308 bullet about 27 cm <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. The ballistics session has the table.</li><li>Write the number on the tape inside your scope cap. Test again each season and after any change of scope, rings or load (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"checklist\" data-list=\"s5-range-test\"><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s5-range-test:0\"><span>20 cm circle targets, 4 of them</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s5-range-test:1\"><span>Timer on phone, 90 seconds</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s5-range-test:2\"><span>Sticks or the rest I will carry</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s5-range-test:3\"><span>12 rounds of my hunting load, cold barrel</span></label><label class=\"check\"><input type=\"checkbox\" data-key=\"s5-range-test:4\"><span>Result written in the journal: distance, position, wind</span></label></div>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bench only</td><td>Practise sitting and sticks</td></tr><tr><td>Ammo on the dry fire table</td><td>No ammo in the room</td></tr><tr><td>Offhand when sitting was 1 second away</td><td>Say the position out loud</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>If you can't hit a paper plate, you can't hit a deer. The plate doesn't walk away.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Before the shot, say the position out loud: \"Sitting. Sticks.\" Get into it. Then find the animal again in the scope.</p></aside><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: 3 common mistakes</summary><ul><li>Practising only from the bench, then meeting a deer with no bench in sight.</li><li>Dry firing with a box of ammunition on the same table.</li><li>Shooting offhand when sitting was one second away.</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>8 sources, checked 2026-10-01. Hunter education 85%, Tikka manual 95%.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all sources</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.hunter-ed.com/national/studyGuide/Firing-Positions-Prone/201099_92888/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hunter Ed: firing positions, prone</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.hunter-ed.com/national/studyGuide/Firing-Positions-Sitting/201099_92890/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hunter Ed: firing positions, sitting</a>, <a href=\"https://www.hunter-ed.com/national/studyGuide/Firing-Positions-Kneeling/201099_92891/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">kneeling</a>, <a href=\"https://www.hunter-ed.com/national/studyGuide/Firing-Positions-Standing/201099_92889/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">standing</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.hunter-ed.com/national/studyGuide/Rifle-Firing-Techniques/201099_92887/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hunter Ed: rifle firing techniques</a> and <a href=\"https://www.hunter-ed.com/muzzleloader/studyGuide/Rifle-Firing-Techniques-Practicing-the-Five-Fundamentals/222099_88875/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">the five fundamentals</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://media.sako.global/image/upload/v1691658741/Tikka_T1x_T3x_Instruction_Manual_v5.3_cjggnu.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Tikka T1x and T3x instruction manual, v5.3, page 9, dry firing</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://fieldandstream.com/stories/hunting/how-to-use-shooting-sticks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Field and Stream: how to use shooting sticks from standing, Richard Mann</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.americanhunter.org/content/best-shooting-rests-for-hunters/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">American Hunter: best shooting rests for hunters</a>, read directly, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.americanhunter.org/content/learn-your-maximum-point-blank-range/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">American Hunter: learn your maximum point blank range, Ron Spomer</a>, hard and soft rests, vital zone sizes, read directly, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li><li>Dry fire steps, the four week plan and the max range test: Hunt Mentor's own method, opinion.</li></ul></details>"]